WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.770
(light music)

00:00:01.770 --> 00:00:04.030
- I was told give up and I have to live

00:00:04.030 --> 00:00:06.640
with my red discoloration
on half of my face

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:07.873
for the rest of my life.

00:00:10.150 --> 00:00:12.830
I felt like I don't want
to give up on myself.

00:00:12.830 --> 00:00:15.083
I'm gonna go out there
and find a solution.

00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:18.420
My name is Basma Hameed,
and I help people heal

00:00:18.420 --> 00:00:19.913
from the inside out.

00:00:25.532 --> 00:00:27.850
(playful music)

00:00:27.850 --> 00:00:30.460
I am a micropigmentation specialist.

00:00:30.460 --> 00:00:35.100
I camouflage all types of
scars, birth marks, and burns.

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:37.600
I implant pigment and scar tissue

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:40.053
to eliminate any
discoloration in the skin.

00:00:41.750 --> 00:00:43.630
When I was two years old, I
was playing in the kitchen

00:00:43.630 --> 00:00:46.510
with my brother, and a fire started.

00:00:46.510 --> 00:00:50.143
Hot oil ended up spilling
on 50% of my face.

00:00:51.820 --> 00:00:54.244
I ended up with third-degree burns.

00:00:54.244 --> 00:00:59.244
I've had almost 100 types of
surgeries and laser treatments.

00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:02.090
None of them were successful.

00:01:02.090 --> 00:01:04.340
I went to talk to my plastic surgeon.

00:01:04.340 --> 00:01:05.930
I asked him, "What can I do?"

00:01:05.930 --> 00:01:07.567
He said, "Just take your money.

00:01:07.567 --> 00:01:08.827
"Go on a vacation.

00:01:08.827 --> 00:01:10.067
"This is the end for you.

00:01:10.067 --> 00:01:11.447
"We can't improve it."

00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:14.497
I said, "What about permanent cosmetics?

00:01:14.497 --> 00:01:16.390
"Can I get my eyebrow tattooed?"

00:01:16.390 --> 00:01:18.818
He said, "It's the worst
thing you can do for yourself.

00:01:18.818 --> 00:01:21.917
"Scar tissue will never pick up pigment."

00:01:22.820 --> 00:01:25.040
That day, I decided I'm gonna go

00:01:25.040 --> 00:01:27.350
and have my eyebrows tattooed.

00:01:27.350 --> 00:01:29.923
My scar tissue picked up the pigment.

00:01:31.297 --> 00:01:32.990
(upbeat music)

00:01:32.990 --> 00:01:36.610
From that moment, I thought
why not make skin tone pigments

00:01:36.610 --> 00:01:39.130
and implant that pigment
in the scar tissue

00:01:39.130 --> 00:01:41.063
to eliminate the discoloration.

00:01:43.480 --> 00:01:46.340
I started apprenticing with
a permanent makeup artist.

00:01:46.340 --> 00:01:50.010
I learned everything that I
needed to know about skin.

00:01:50.010 --> 00:01:54.570
I decided to be my first
client and work on my own face.

00:01:54.570 --> 00:01:58.370
I was able to camouflage
all the red discoloration,

00:01:58.370 --> 00:02:00.763
and I had something that actually worked.

00:02:03.094 --> 00:02:05.020
Originally when I started it,

00:02:05.020 --> 00:02:07.640
I wanted a solution for myself.

00:02:07.640 --> 00:02:10.583
But from there, it had
like a much bigger purpose.

00:02:11.490 --> 00:02:13.470
We have the clinic in Toronto, Canada,

00:02:13.470 --> 00:02:16.160
and we have the clinic
now in Beverly Hills.

00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:18.453
We perform this procedure
every single day.

00:02:19.350 --> 00:02:21.990
Now we reached a point
where plastic surgeons

00:02:21.990 --> 00:02:22.920
reach out to us.

00:02:22.920 --> 00:02:25.440
They want to learn more
about the procedure.

00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:27.760
We've performed thousands of procedures

00:02:27.760 --> 00:02:29.530
in the last 15 years,

00:02:29.530 --> 00:02:32.380
and it's clients that are
flying from all over the world.

00:02:36.190 --> 00:02:38.530
Every year, we take on few big cases,

00:02:38.530 --> 00:02:40.353
and we donate those treatments.

00:02:41.310 --> 00:02:44.560
Adela has a permanent stain on her face.

00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:48.190
She's had so many different
types of treatments.

00:02:48.190 --> 00:02:49.993
Nothing really has worked for her.

00:02:52.620 --> 00:02:54.590
- Very thankful for her too

00:02:54.590 --> 00:02:57.693
'cause she's making my
dream come true, you know?

00:02:58.580 --> 00:03:01.440
I used to use for heavy
makeup to cover enough,

00:03:01.440 --> 00:03:02.850
layer and layer.

00:03:02.850 --> 00:03:04.290
It's a big difference.

00:03:04.290 --> 00:03:06.393
It used to be four times longer.

00:03:08.330 --> 00:03:12.693
- The best part about this,
it's seeing people transform.

00:03:12.693 --> 00:03:16.085
That's why I'm so grateful
that I never gave up.

00:03:16.085 --> 00:03:19.393
On my journey, I was able
to help thousands of people.

